I disagree with your overall optimism here. 79% is not fine, specifically
in the early game. You waste PW points for nothing; those are better spent
for the spells that keep you alife directly, like healing and protection, or
indirectly like light. Stone to flesh on a pile of rocks sucks! They just
don't have enough nutrition. Meatballs are nice for your carnivorous pets,
but that's it. The spell is useful as food supply it applied on boulders,
and at some point you'll probably find some. Not sure what you have in mind
when saying "that you can eat all corpses/rations"; a pet will eat corpses
anyway, even if fed with meatballs, and rations will be left alone by pets,
they're anyway only touched by them if they're close to starvation. You
argument about the spell of identify as if it would be typical to fully
identify your loot, but that is not the case. Early you have not enough PW
to try to cast it often, let alone until a full identification. While it's
an option once you are settled a bit it's not advisable in the early game.
YMMV.

